# Territorial Witchstalker {1}{G} (2/3 defender): "At the beginning of combat on your turn, if you control a creature with power 4 or
# greater, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn and can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender." An intervening "if"
# (CR 603.4). Turn 1: Bot1 casts the Witchstalker and a Centaur Courser (power 3, just short): no trigger, power stays 2. Turn 3: an
# Alpine Grizzly (power 4 exactly) is cast first, so the Witchstalker becomes a 3/3 that attacks despite defender. Turn 5: Bot2 bolts
# the Grizzly in response to the combat trigger, so the condition fails on resolution (checked again, CR 603.4): no pump, and the
# Witchstalker (defender, power 2) can't attack.

